/-!
# The Lee–Pomeransky polynomial of the set (d) family: literal, derivatives, positivity

`G = U + F` of the three-loop family `QED.ThreeLoopD.SetDCert.lbl` (`QED.DimReg.ThreeLoop.lpPoly`)
as a literal sparse polynomial (`lpPoly_eq_lit`, `decide +kernel`; generated by `uf.py` and
compared with an independent sympy computation of `det A` and `Bᵀ adj(A) B`), its partial
degrees `degs = (1, 1, 1, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 1)` (`deg_lpPoly`), its partial derivatives
`gD b = ∂_b G` (`hasDerivAt_G`, computed on exponents by `QED.DimReg.ZPoly.diff`) and its
positivity on the orthant (`G_pos`). These are the inputs of
`QED.DimReg.lpIntegral_annihilator` and of the continuation for the family.
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace QED.DimReg.ThreeLoop

